  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reducing Forced Labor in Costa Rica&#x2019;s Fishing Industry</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the baseline prevalence survey and gap analysis, this John Jay-IOM team will obtain a detailed picture of the current state of human trafficking in the fishing sector in Puntarenas, its nature and scope, service needs, and communities amenable to interventions. Based on the findings of this research, the project team and key partners will select 3-5 communities to participate in a counter-trafficking intervention program.</narrative>
  </description>
